1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:02,700
(EP02 Behind-the-Scenes)

2
00:00:02,740 --> 00:00:05,980
(Behind-the-Scenes 1)

3
00:00:08,060 --> 00:00:09,300
Have you played basketball before?

4
00:00:09,590 --> 00:00:10,940
I played in elementary school.

5
00:00:10,940 --> 00:00:11,780
Does that count?

6
00:00:12,060 --> 00:00:12,860
It counts.

7
00:00:13,940 --> 00:00:14,900
Your turn.

8
00:00:15,540 --> 00:00:17,140
Let me give it a try.

9
00:00:18,750 --> 00:00:20,140
I can pick up the ball for you.

10
00:00:20,260 --> 00:00:21,660
I can pick up the ball for you.

11
00:00:22,020 --> 00:00:22,860
(Missed)

12
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:23,780
It's all right.

13
00:00:23,780 --> 00:00:25,070
I'll try again.

14
00:00:26,740 --> 00:00:27,340
(Made the shot)

15
00:00:28,710 --> 00:00:30,150
A highlight moment.

16
00:00:31,540 --> 00:00:32,500
All right, your turn.

17
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:34,620
(Asks)
Is there a technique to this?

18
00:00:35,140 --> 00:00:37,220
You just jump and throw it.

19
00:00:37,220 --> 00:00:38,380
(Demonstrates)

20
00:00:40,030 --> 00:00:40,980
Come a little closer.

21
00:00:42,580 --> 00:00:43,540
Okay.

22
00:00:43,550 --> 00:00:44,140
It feels...

23
00:00:44,140 --> 00:00:44,820
Do it like this.

24
00:00:47,470 --> 00:00:49,830
When I was first learning,
I did it this way too.

25
00:00:49,830 --> 00:00:53,030
You just throw the ball.

26
00:00:55,420 --> 00:00:56,740
Am I too short?

27
00:00:56,740 --> 00:00:57,870
You can move a little closer.

28
00:00:58,140 --> 00:00:59,660
(Hands it over)

29
00:00:59,910 --> 00:01:01,270
Right here

30
00:01:01,270 --> 00:01:02,190
should be fine.

31
00:01:02,230 --> 00:01:03,430
Come a little closer.

32
00:01:04,140 --> 00:01:04,940
Like this?

33
00:01:05,230 --> 00:01:07,030
Yes, or here.

34
00:01:07,420 --> 00:01:08,220
Here?

35
00:01:08,660 --> 00:01:10,070
Beginners usually start from here,

36
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:12,460
then aim for that white square

37
00:01:12,460 --> 00:01:13,620
and the ball will go in.

38
00:01:14,380 --> 00:01:15,860
(Moves closer)

39
00:01:16,030 --> 00:01:17,510
You can shoot

40
00:01:17,510 --> 00:01:19,430
from this distance.

41
00:01:19,430 --> 00:01:20,150
For me, even with my arm

42
00:01:20,150 --> 00:01:22,220
fully extended,
I can only reach your head.

43
00:01:22,220 --> 00:01:23,420
It's actually about the same.

44
00:01:25,300 --> 00:01:26,500
It's much easier to make the shot.

45
00:01:29,940 --> 00:01:30,980
All right,

46
00:01:31,230 --> 00:01:31,860
that's it.

47
00:01:31,860 --> 00:01:32,780
That's it.

48
00:01:35,420 --> 00:01:36,140
Okay.

49
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:42,860
(Behind-the-Scenes 2)

50
00:01:42,900 --> 00:01:44,700
(After the newcomers' dinner)

51
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:46,740
So, how do you usually

52
00:01:46,740 --> 00:01:47,660
get to work? By taxi?

53
00:01:47,660 --> 00:01:48,660
I usually take a taxi.

54
00:01:48,660 --> 00:01:50,260
I take one there and back.

55
00:01:50,260 --> 00:01:50,940
Is it far?

56
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:53,340
It takes about an hour.

57
00:01:54,030 --> 00:01:55,140
Since you study psychology,

58
00:01:55,140 --> 00:01:56,740
is your brain now

59
00:01:56,740 --> 00:01:58,260
like a ball of yarn?

60
00:01:58,260 --> 00:01:59,180
All tightly wound.

61
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:00,100
I've already

62
00:02:00,100 --> 00:02:01,620
analyzed you pretty thoroughly.

63
00:02:01,620 --> 00:02:02,500
(Joking)

64
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:03,950
What kind of person do you think I am?

65
00:02:05,310 --> 00:02:08,110
I think you're a rather
sensitive person.

66
00:02:08,110 --> 00:02:08,780
Do you

67
00:02:08,780 --> 00:02:09,420
think so?

68
00:02:09,580 --> 00:02:10,900
(Nods)
Yes, definitely.

69
00:02:14,470 --> 00:02:16,030
(Curious)
How'd you know?

70
00:02:16,660 --> 00:02:18,180
I can sense it.

71
00:02:18,750 --> 00:02:19,590
Just a feeling?

72
00:02:20,660 --> 00:02:21,780
With many things in daily life,

73
00:02:21,780 --> 00:02:22,900
do you tend to have worries,

74
00:02:22,900 --> 00:02:24,140
or can you see through everything

75
00:02:24,140 --> 00:02:25,870
and make sense of it all?

76
00:02:26,710 --> 00:02:28,390
I still have quite a lot of worries.

77
00:02:28,540 --> 00:02:29,500
What kind of worries?

78
00:02:31,060 --> 00:02:32,180
(Laughs)

79
00:02:32,220 --> 00:02:33,340
I'll keep it confidential.

80
00:02:36,470 --> 00:02:37,310
It's nothing, really.

81
00:02:37,670 --> 00:02:38,500
I just feel that everyone

82
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:39,940
seems to have integrated so quickly.

83
00:02:40,540 --> 00:02:41,620
You're more

84
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:42,260
slow to warm up.

85
00:02:42,260 --> 00:02:44,500
So I feel a little pressured, too.

86
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:46,620
It feels like you haven't quite fit in.

87
00:02:49,710 --> 00:02:51,230
When will we get to hear you sing?

88
00:02:52,470 --> 00:02:54,060
I'll let everyone hear me someday.

89
00:02:54,420 --> 00:02:55,220
(Laughs)
All right.

90
00:02:55,670 --> 00:02:57,230
I imagine it must sound wonderful.

91
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:06,460
(Behind-the-Scenes 3)

92
00:03:08,740 --> 00:03:10,070
When I first met you, I wanted to ask,

93
00:03:10,070 --> 00:03:11,100
are you tired?

94
00:03:11,100 --> 00:03:12,260
(Could I?)
Would you be willing

95
00:03:12,260 --> 00:03:14,660
(Would you?)
to take a walk with me?

96
00:03:16,100 --> 00:03:17,940
I said I'd walk three laps
outside your door,

97
00:03:17,940 --> 00:03:19,190
then three laps downstairs.

98
00:03:22,140 --> 00:03:23,100
After three laps downstairs,

99
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:24,220
I'd do three more outside your room.

100
00:03:24,220 --> 00:03:24,980
I mean...

101
00:03:25,180 --> 00:03:26,700
I don't even know what I was doing.

102
00:03:30,350 --> 00:03:31,190
What about me?

103
00:03:31,190 --> 00:03:32,500
(Asks)
What do you think of me?

104
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:33,460
You're quite nice.

105
00:03:33,700 --> 00:03:34,700
(Quite nice)
You're quite nice.

106
00:03:38,510 --> 00:03:39,270
I think...

107
00:03:40,390 --> 00:03:41,630
you have a beautiful smile.

108
00:03:41,630 --> 00:03:42,390
You should smile more.

109
00:03:45,740 --> 00:03:46,900
Your smile is very infectious.

110
00:03:46,900 --> 00:03:47,910
It's so easy

111
00:03:47,910 --> 00:03:48,510
for my gaze

112
00:03:48,510 --> 00:03:50,220
to be drawn toward you unconsciously.

113
00:03:50,220 --> 00:03:50,700
Yes.

114
00:03:51,900 --> 00:03:53,100
Really.

115
00:03:56,270 --> 00:03:57,710
Why are you shy about compliments again?

116
00:03:58,030 --> 00:03:59,750
I didn't smile much yesterday.

117
00:04:00,070 --> 00:04:00,790
You didn't smile much

118
00:04:00,790 --> 00:04:01,940
yesterday. So, can you smile

119
00:04:01,940 --> 00:04:02,980
more every day

120
00:04:03,470 --> 00:04:03,870
from now on?

121
00:04:04,380 --> 00:04:06,260
(Stares)

122
00:04:09,150 --> 00:04:09,750
There it is again.

123
00:04:09,750 --> 00:04:10,110
Yes.

124
00:04:10,950 --> 00:04:11,750
(Shy)
What is happening?

125
00:04:12,390 --> 00:04:14,150
It seems that when I speak,
I can activate

126
00:04:15,270 --> 00:04:15,950
your smiling switch,

127
00:04:15,950 --> 00:04:16,340
right?

128
00:04:16,340 --> 00:04:17,060
Yes.

129
00:04:21,300 --> 00:04:26,260
(Behind-the-Scenes 4)

130
00:04:26,300 --> 00:04:27,820
(Signal House)

131
00:04:27,820 --> 00:04:29,190
Would you like to play some pool?

132
00:04:29,190 --> 00:04:29,980
Sure.

133
00:04:46,390 --> 00:04:47,190
This...

134
00:04:47,190 --> 00:04:47,900
(Very close)

135
00:04:49,060 --> 00:04:50,500
There's no bridge?

136
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:52,820
No. It only has an extension.

137
00:04:52,820 --> 00:04:54,300
(Extension cue)
It only has an extension.

138
00:04:58,500 --> 00:05:00,620
(Uses it as a bridge manually)

139
00:05:03,180 --> 00:05:04,060
All right.

140
00:05:09,740 --> 00:05:10,540
(Perfect shot)
Perfect.

141
00:05:12,940 --> 00:05:14,140
(Happy)

142
00:05:14,140 --> 00:05:14,940
Come on.

143
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:20,260
(Hits the black ball)

144
00:05:20,260 --> 00:05:20,660
I'm sorry.

145
00:05:20,660 --> 00:05:21,380
I moved it.

146
00:05:21,540 --> 00:05:22,580
Go ahead.

147
00:05:22,740 --> 00:05:23,420
I've moved it.

148
00:05:24,100 --> 00:05:24,940
Go on.

149
00:05:25,620 --> 00:05:26,900
It's all right.

150
00:05:32,140 --> 00:05:33,460
(Gently taps it)

151
00:05:34,500 --> 00:05:36,300
(Thinking)

152
00:05:41,860 --> 00:05:42,700
(White ball is pocketed)

153
00:05:43,980 --> 00:05:45,020
Free ball?

154
00:05:45,340 --> 00:05:46,300
Free ball.

155
00:05:49,860 --> 00:05:50,780
No problem.

156
00:05:50,780 --> 00:05:51,830
Sure.

157
00:05:53,740 --> 00:05:58,700
(Behind-the-Scenes 5)

158
00:05:59,710 --> 00:06:01,470
If only we had a scale.

159
00:06:01,990 --> 00:06:04,230
To be honest, I'd like
to weigh myself, too.

160
00:06:04,540 --> 00:06:05,580
I'm extremely thin.

161
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:07,860
I have to tuck in my shirt just to keep

162
00:06:07,860 --> 00:06:08,980
my pants from falling.

163
00:06:09,190 --> 00:06:10,430
Same here.

164
00:06:11,220 --> 00:06:12,460
You may have a low body-fat percentage.

165
00:06:12,910 --> 00:06:14,300
You're just thin.

166
00:06:14,300 --> 00:06:14,780
Yes.

167
00:06:15,180 --> 00:06:16,620
My body-fat percentage is quite high.

168
00:06:16,900 --> 00:06:18,980
Even my flesh
feels very soft to the touch.

169
00:06:19,190 --> 00:06:21,030
I just don't have much muscle mass.

170
00:06:21,030 --> 00:06:21,400
(Pinches)

171
00:06:21,400 --> 00:06:22,670
You probably have more muscle than me.

172
00:06:22,670 --> 00:06:24,110
(Listens)
I think mine is slightly...

173
00:06:24,740 --> 00:06:26,500
I think my body-fat percentage
is higher than yours.

174
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:28,060
I weigh over 130 jin now.

175
00:06:28,140 --> 00:06:29,220
(Seriously)
Yes, over 130 jin now.

176
00:06:29,220 --> 00:06:29,820
Yes.

177
00:06:32,990 --> 00:06:33,710
You...

178
00:06:35,780 --> 00:06:37,340
We do have a gym here, don't we?

179
00:06:37,820 --> 00:06:39,780
At the very least,
you could lift some dumbbells.

180
00:06:40,140 --> 00:06:41,340
I could try lifting them sometime.

181
00:06:41,340 --> 00:06:42,020
Yes.

182
00:06:42,020 --> 00:06:43,110
You can use them while lying down.

183
00:06:43,110 --> 00:06:44,380
You can work your chest, shoulders,

184
00:06:44,380 --> 00:06:46,100
biceps and triceps.

185
00:06:46,100 --> 00:06:48,300
But you have to make sure
to eat enough protein afterward.

186
00:06:48,710 --> 00:06:50,150
Otherwise the workout
would be pointless.

187
00:06:52,270 --> 00:06:53,750
Never mind. I'll take out
my contacts first.

188
00:06:54,700 --> 00:06:55,740
(Takes a look)

189
00:06:58,110 --> 00:06:59,230
Are these contacts uncomfortable?

190
00:06:59,870 --> 00:07:00,940
Daily disposables are comfortable.

191
00:07:01,100 --> 00:07:02,030
Daily disposables are comfortable.

192
00:07:02,580 --> 00:07:03,540
Take a look.

193
00:07:04,660 --> 00:07:06,220
(Curious)

194
00:07:06,420 --> 00:07:07,660
(Carefully examines)

195
00:07:08,140 --> 00:07:09,420
These look quite stylish.

196
00:07:09,470 --> 00:07:10,260
Very striking.

197
00:07:10,380 --> 00:07:11,340
Yes.

198
00:07:12,100 --> 00:07:17,060
(Behind-the-Scenes 6)

199
00:07:19,340 --> 00:07:20,940
Do you like going to amusement parks?

200
00:07:21,140 --> 00:07:21,940
I do.

201
00:07:22,540 --> 00:07:23,540
I think we'd have a lot of fun

202
00:07:23,540 --> 00:07:24,300
at the park together.

203
00:07:24,300 --> 00:07:24,940
It should be fun.

204
00:07:24,940 --> 00:07:25,500
Yes.

205
00:07:25,900 --> 00:07:26,580
(Agrees)

206
00:07:26,580 --> 00:07:28,110
At first, Si seems quiet and reserved,

207
00:07:28,110 --> 00:07:28,630
so it's surprising.

208
00:07:28,630 --> 00:07:29,380
But she likes things...

209
00:07:29,380 --> 00:07:30,190
That get your adrenaline pumping.

210
00:07:30,190 --> 00:07:30,870
That are more thrilling.

211
00:07:31,270 --> 00:07:32,020
Yes.

212
00:07:32,020 --> 00:07:33,020
When she asked that,

213
00:07:33,020 --> 00:07:33,910
I knew she liked them.

214
00:07:34,260 --> 00:07:35,190
(Smiles)

215
00:07:35,190 --> 00:07:36,000
(Asks)

216
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,230
Ever been on an upside-down ride?

217
00:07:37,340 --> 00:07:38,140
Yes.

218
00:07:38,790 --> 00:07:39,710
So you are not afraid?

219
00:07:40,630 --> 00:07:41,470
I was at first.

220
00:07:41,470 --> 00:07:43,110
But after going on one, I realized

221
00:07:43,420 --> 00:07:45,020
that the only frightening part
was getting on.

222
00:07:45,020 --> 00:07:47,100
But I actually find
the pirate ship pretty scary.

223
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:47,660
(Agrees)

224
00:07:47,750 --> 00:07:49,860
When I was little,

225
00:07:49,860 --> 00:07:51,980
I would just cry on the pirate ship.

226
00:07:52,460 --> 00:07:54,180
(Laughs)

227
00:07:55,180 --> 00:07:56,340
And it would not stop,

228
00:07:56,340 --> 00:07:57,900
so I would just keep crying
the whole time.

229
00:08:01,990 --> 00:08:03,060
Ever been to an amusement park

230
00:08:03,060 --> 00:08:04,540
(looks)
for those Halloween events?

231
00:08:05,060 --> 00:08:06,100
I have.

232
00:08:06,220 --> 00:08:06,940
There was a haunted house.

233
00:08:07,110 --> 00:08:09,590
I'm not good at escape rooms,

234
00:08:09,590 --> 00:08:10,590
especially single-path ones.

235
00:08:12,380 --> 00:08:13,380
(Asks)
Si, would you dare to do one?

236
00:08:14,540 --> 00:08:15,900
I think I would.

237
00:08:16,420 --> 00:08:17,340
You are quite brave.

238
00:08:17,340 --> 00:08:17,940
(Praises)

239
00:08:17,950 --> 00:08:18,630
I wonder if we'll

240
00:08:18,630 --> 00:08:20,030
have a chance to go together someday.

241
00:08:20,230 --> 00:08:21,350
Of course we will.

242
00:08:21,660 --> 00:08:22,220
Yes.

243
00:08:23,780 --> 00:08:28,740
(Behind-the-Scenes 7)

244
00:08:29,540 --> 00:08:31,300
(Cao Yiheng, Cui Kaiyi, 1-on-1 Date)
I feel like this one's less scary.

245
00:08:31,910 --> 00:08:33,710
Yes, there is more protection
on this one.

246
00:08:33,710 --> 00:08:34,500
(Pulls)
Yes, this one's less scary

247
00:08:34,900 --> 00:08:36,630
(Supports)
than the last one.

248
00:08:37,380 --> 00:08:38,500
Are you up yet?

249
00:08:38,500 --> 00:08:39,340
Not yet.

250
00:08:39,510 --> 00:08:40,230
Let me steady it for you.

251
00:08:40,230 --> 00:08:41,070
Then come on up.

252
00:08:41,220 --> 00:08:42,940
Okay.

253
00:08:42,980 --> 00:08:44,420
(Shaking)

254
00:08:44,870 --> 00:08:46,390
It really shakes once you get up there.

255
00:08:47,020 --> 00:08:49,020
(Supports)

256
00:08:51,150 --> 00:08:52,030
We made it across.

257
00:08:52,420 --> 00:08:54,660
(Follows)

258
00:08:55,300 --> 00:08:56,700
It really shakes once you get up there.

259
00:08:57,100 --> 00:08:58,340
That just scared me half to death.

260
00:08:58,630 --> 00:09:00,190
Do you know why I am behind you?

261
00:09:00,310 --> 00:09:00,870
Why?

262
00:09:00,870 --> 00:09:02,870
Because this is specifically
for filming you.

263
00:09:03,030 --> 00:09:04,260
Specifically for filming you.

264
00:09:05,100 --> 00:09:06,700
Then can you make me look good?

265
00:09:07,100 --> 00:09:08,500
Of course.

266
00:09:11,220 --> 00:09:12,300
(Afraid)

267
00:09:12,460 --> 00:09:13,580
(Offers advice)
Place your feet sideways.

268
00:09:14,020 --> 00:09:14,980
Are you up yet?

269
00:09:14,980 --> 00:09:15,860
Should I come up?

270
00:09:16,140 --> 00:09:17,140
You...

271
00:09:17,700 --> 00:09:18,900
You...

272
00:09:19,500 --> 00:09:20,900
(Shaking)

273
00:09:21,030 --> 00:09:23,070
It's all right. I'll put one foot down
for a moment.

274
00:09:23,070 --> 00:09:23,950
Let you feel it.

275
00:09:23,980 --> 00:09:25,980
(Testing)

276
00:09:26,660 --> 00:09:27,740
It is a little shaky.

277
00:09:27,740 --> 00:09:28,420
Is it all right?

278
00:09:28,420 --> 00:09:29,220
It's manageable.

279
00:09:30,230 --> 00:09:32,310
Place your foot on the cross.

280
00:09:32,310 --> 00:09:33,470
The center is more stable.

281
00:09:33,590 --> 00:09:34,350
Indeed.

282
00:09:35,460 --> 00:09:36,700
This is much steadier.

283
00:09:36,900 --> 00:09:38,820
I can walk confidently now.

284
00:09:39,030 --> 00:09:40,750
Yes, it is still quite shaky for me.

285
00:09:41,580 --> 00:09:43,180
(Easily makes it across)

286
00:09:45,750 --> 00:09:48,070
That was nothing. It's fine.

287
00:09:49,220 --> 00:09:50,740
What should we do?
I cannot get past this.

288
00:09:50,740 --> 00:09:51,300
(Stuck)

289
00:09:53,510 --> 00:09:54,180
Watch your head.

290
00:09:56,940 --> 00:09:58,020
Okay, that's it.

291
00:10:00,820 --> 00:10:05,780
(Behind-the-Scenes 8)

292
00:10:05,880 --> 00:10:07,220
(Sun Qimeng, Zhao Xilun:
The Courageous Date)

293
00:10:07,350 --> 00:10:09,990
What do you think you are really like?

294
00:10:10,150 --> 00:10:11,620
(Quirky)
I am actually quite quirky myself.

295
00:10:11,620 --> 00:10:12,780
But your kind of quirkiness

296
00:10:12,780 --> 00:10:14,990
seems to be a little stronger than mine.

297
00:10:15,340 --> 00:10:17,260
I think being quirky
is a kind of attitude.

298
00:10:17,260 --> 00:10:18,460
Deep down,

299
00:10:18,460 --> 00:10:20,350
everyone has a tendency

300
00:10:20,350 --> 00:10:22,590
to want to break the rules.

301
00:10:23,620 --> 00:10:24,940
For example, today,

302
00:10:24,940 --> 00:10:25,700
after school,

303
00:10:25,700 --> 00:10:27,030
I might plan to ride my bicycle home,

304
00:10:27,430 --> 00:10:29,270
but I would insist on stopping
by a convenience store first.

305
00:10:29,740 --> 00:10:31,140
I would not ride somewhere far away,

306
00:10:31,140 --> 00:10:32,340
but I would take a detour.

307
00:10:32,900 --> 00:10:33,580
That is what I mean.

308
00:10:33,580 --> 00:10:35,300
I think everyone probably has that side.

309
00:10:38,190 --> 00:10:39,550
(Brave)
I think you are very brave.

310
00:10:41,100 --> 00:10:42,100
Really.

311
00:10:42,390 --> 00:10:43,420
But you are braver.

312
00:10:43,420 --> 00:10:44,900
(Playful)
I am just being playful.

313
00:10:45,500 --> 00:10:47,750
I think brave

314
00:10:47,750 --> 00:10:49,150
is a very meaningful word.

315
00:10:49,950 --> 00:10:52,750
Yes, because I have always
wanted to be brave.

316
00:10:53,870 --> 00:10:55,350
But you already are.

317
00:10:59,260 --> 00:11:04,220
(Behind-the-Scenes 9)

318
00:11:04,260 --> 00:11:06,260
(After the five-person group date)

319
00:11:06,260 --> 00:11:09,550
I was watching "Love Trilogy"
a couple of days ago.

320
00:11:10,620 --> 00:11:10,999
I think

321
00:11:10,999 --> 00:11:12,300
(Listens attentively)
it is similar to life in the house.

322
00:11:12,300 --> 00:11:12,990
Don't you think so?

323
00:11:13,460 --> 00:11:16,820
Getting to know someone

324
00:11:16,820 --> 00:11:17,940
through conversation.

325
00:11:17,940 --> 00:11:18,790
Getting to know someone...

326
00:11:18,860 --> 00:11:20,020
Do you like talking?

327
00:11:20,140 --> 00:11:21,100
I love talking.

328
00:11:21,100 --> 00:11:21,990
(Repeats)
Love talking.

329
00:11:22,300 --> 00:11:24,980
But it can be exhausting.

330
00:11:26,060 --> 00:11:26,940
Everyone feels

331
00:11:26,940 --> 00:11:27,660
that way sometimes.

332
00:11:28,140 --> 00:11:28,420
Yes.

333
00:11:28,420 --> 00:11:29,900
Everyone needs time to recharge.

334
00:11:29,900 --> 00:11:30,700
Yes.

335
00:11:31,300 --> 00:11:32,700
How do you usually recharge?

336
00:11:33,140 --> 00:11:34,460
(Thinks)

337
00:11:34,460 --> 00:11:36,070
Staying at home and watching shows.

338
00:11:37,100 --> 00:11:39,060
I actually love traveling.

339
00:11:39,580 --> 00:11:40,340
Me too.

340
00:11:40,340 --> 00:11:41,380
I absolutely love traveling.

341
00:11:42,700 --> 00:11:43,900
Have you been to Chongqing?

342
00:11:45,110 --> 00:11:45,790
I have.

343
00:11:45,790 --> 00:11:46,750
I go to Chongqing quite often.

344
00:11:47,700 --> 00:11:50,620
The roads in Chongqing really
are a little difficult

345
00:11:50,620 --> 00:11:51,500
to navigate.

346
00:11:52,180 --> 00:11:53,300
(Laughs)

347
00:11:53,300 --> 00:11:54,380
They are so confusing.

348
00:11:54,380 --> 00:11:56,540
You can walk up ten floors
and still find yourself

349
00:11:56,540 --> 00:11:57,500
on the first floor.

350
00:11:57,500 --> 00:11:59,140
Yes.

351
00:11:59,140 --> 00:12:01,030
So, in our building, the first floor
is still the first floor,

352
00:12:01,030 --> 00:12:02,390
and the third floor
is also the first floor.

353
00:12:03,020 --> 00:12:04,860
Our food deliveries are always
sent to the wrong place.

354
00:12:06,020 --> 00:12:08,500
(Look at each other and laugh)

355
00:12:10,180 --> 00:12:15,140
(Behind-the-Scenes 10)

356
00:12:15,140 --> 00:12:17,330
(Signal House)
One of the courageous has gone out.

357
00:12:18,550 --> 00:12:19,710
What about the guys?

358
00:12:19,780 --> 00:12:20,540
I have no idea.

359
00:12:20,540 --> 00:12:21,460
Just wait.

360
00:12:22,140 --> 00:12:24,260
Wait for the judgment of fate.

361
00:12:25,150 --> 00:12:26,020
You know what's funny?

362
00:12:26,020 --> 00:12:27,140
What if the courageous

363
00:12:27,140 --> 00:12:28,430
and the newcomer chose the same person?

364
00:12:29,110 --> 00:12:30,550
Then they can just
go on a date together.

365
00:12:32,060 --> 00:12:32,780
(Is that possible?)

366
00:12:32,880 --> 00:12:33,500
The female courageous

367
00:12:33,500 --> 00:12:35,060
(Analyzing)
has chosen a guy,

368
00:12:35,430 --> 00:12:36,870
and the newcomer has also chosen a guy.

369
00:12:36,870 --> 00:12:39,420
If the newcomer
and one or two courageous

370
00:12:39,420 --> 00:12:40,980
choose the same person,

371
00:12:40,980 --> 00:12:41,980
that's too much of a coincidence.

372
00:12:41,980 --> 00:12:42,660
Three people picking one?

373
00:12:42,660 --> 00:12:43,460
That is impossible.

374
00:12:43,460 --> 00:12:44,340
They have to pick someone else.

375
00:12:44,460 --> 00:12:45,620
Two people fighting over one person.

376
00:12:45,620 --> 00:12:46,780
But I doubt that would happen either.

377
00:12:46,780 --> 00:12:48,900
It is possible that the three girls
chose three different guys.

378
00:12:49,340 --> 00:12:51,300
I think you two are probably
the two courageous.

379
00:12:52,180 --> 00:12:53,260
Are we really that brave?

380
00:12:53,420 --> 00:12:54,500
Because everyone
has someone to root for.

381
00:12:54,500 --> 00:12:55,020
Yes.

382
00:12:57,380 --> 00:12:59,310
I think that is probably it.

383
00:12:59,590 --> 00:13:01,390
Wouldn't we have to see
who reads it fastest?

384
00:13:01,910 --> 00:13:02,470
Everyone sent theirs?

385
00:13:02,470 --> 00:13:03,070
Yes.

386
00:13:03,780 --> 00:13:04,380
Just wait.

387
00:13:07,620 --> 00:13:12,540
(Behind-the-Scenes 11)

388
00:13:13,420 --> 00:13:15,950
So, when you are under a lot
of pressure, what do you do?

389
00:13:18,540 --> 00:13:19,340
Sleep?

390
00:13:19,740 --> 00:13:22,540
Yes, sleep, watch shows,
things like that.

391
00:13:22,790 --> 00:13:23,950
Yes. Find my own outlet.

392
00:13:23,950 --> 00:13:24,870
Regulate my emotions myself.

393
00:13:25,150 --> 00:13:28,190
But it'd be better with someone
to help me through it.

394
00:13:33,870 --> 00:13:36,710
Don't you like watching sunrises

395
00:13:36,710 --> 00:13:37,270
and sunsets?

396
00:13:37,660 --> 00:13:39,300
Yes. Actually, whenever
I am on the road,

397
00:13:39,300 --> 00:13:42,060
I always pay attention
to the sunset outside.

398
00:13:42,500 --> 00:13:43,660
Let's go watch

399
00:13:44,110 --> 00:13:45,150
the sunset sometime.

400
00:13:48,900 --> 00:13:50,860
I have many photos
of sunrises and sunsets.

401
00:13:51,030 --> 00:13:52,310
Show them to me when you get back.

402
00:13:52,390 --> 00:13:53,190
Sure.

403
00:13:53,350 --> 00:13:54,700
Do you usually watch it?

404
00:13:54,700 --> 00:13:55,500
I do.

405
00:13:55,500 --> 00:13:56,710
But I don't watch it...

406
00:13:57,820 --> 00:13:58,980
that often.

407
00:13:58,980 --> 00:14:01,620
I don't have an eye for beauty like you.

408
00:14:02,420 --> 00:14:03,660
An eye for beauty.

409
00:14:03,660 --> 00:14:05,100
(You have an eye for beauty)

410
00:14:07,260 --> 00:14:08,340
(Slide)

411
00:14:09,900 --> 00:14:14,860
(Behind-the-Scenes 12)

412
00:14:14,900 --> 00:14:17,060
(After the Newcomers' Dinner)

413
00:14:17,060 --> 00:14:17,630
Today,

414
00:14:17,830 --> 00:14:19,230
when I came out to meet everyone,

415
00:14:19,270 --> 00:14:21,540
I really wanted to get to know

416
00:14:21,540 --> 00:14:22,860
what everyone was like.

417
00:14:22,860 --> 00:14:23,860
And I feel like everyone

418
00:14:23,860 --> 00:14:25,430
is wonderful.

419
00:14:26,470 --> 00:14:27,710
And everyone's so beautiful.

420
00:14:28,270 --> 00:14:29,310
You're very beautiful.

421
00:14:30,900 --> 00:14:32,260
And you sing so well too.

422
00:14:32,620 --> 00:14:33,460
Thank you.

423
00:14:35,310 --> 00:14:37,310
You were probably nervous
before you came, right?

424
00:14:38,350 --> 00:14:39,390
A little nervous.

425
00:14:39,670 --> 00:14:42,150
It all felt so unfamiliar.

426
00:14:43,740 --> 00:14:47,750
I was just curious about what
would happen in the house,

427
00:14:47,750 --> 00:14:49,790
and what everyone would be
doing when they got back.

428
00:14:50,220 --> 00:14:51,420
You'll find out soon enough.

429
00:14:52,660 --> 00:14:53,340
When you get to the house,

430
00:14:53,340 --> 00:14:54,420
I can show you around.

431
00:14:54,420 --> 00:14:55,780
I'll show you around

432
00:14:55,780 --> 00:14:56,700
and explain what each corner is for.

433
00:14:58,710 --> 00:14:59,590
Do you have any luggage?

434
00:15:00,100 --> 00:15:01,340
Just a small suitcase.

435
00:15:01,750 --> 00:15:02,860
I'll help you take it upstairs later.

436
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:03,380
Thank you.

437
00:15:03,380 --> 00:15:04,180
No problem.

438
00:15:06,460 --> 00:15:11,420
(Behind-the-Scenes 13)

439
00:15:15,700 --> 00:15:16,860
(Taking out a memory card)

440
00:15:22,110 --> 00:15:23,460
Is this the new guitar
Liang Renfang bought?

441
00:15:23,460 --> 00:15:24,180
(Liang Renfang's stringless guitar)
Yeah.

442
00:15:24,180 --> 00:15:25,230
She left it here?

443
00:15:25,710 --> 00:15:27,940
I just brought it upstairs
and put it here for her.

444
00:15:28,460 --> 00:15:30,060
It was in the kitchen before.

445
00:15:30,260 --> 00:15:31,140
(Heard a sound)

446
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:33,790
Hello.

447
00:15:34,910 --> 00:15:35,940
(Pointing)
I brought it up.

448
00:15:36,300 --> 00:15:36,980
(Happy)

449
00:15:36,980 --> 00:15:38,380
How did you know I was going to get it?

450
00:15:43,540 --> 00:15:44,900
(Pulling out the memory card)

451
00:15:45,030 --> 00:15:46,110
You found it.

452
00:15:46,390 --> 00:15:47,430
I brought it over so you
could check the photos.

453
00:15:47,580 --> 00:15:48,380
Thank you.

454
00:15:49,230 --> 00:15:49,830
What about the other one?

455
00:15:49,830 --> 00:15:50,670
I'll get it for you.

456
00:15:50,790 --> 00:15:51,470
Okay.

457
00:15:52,900 --> 00:15:55,380
(Looking around)

458
00:15:58,780 --> 00:15:59,780
Found it.

459
00:16:01,270 --> 00:16:02,150
Thank you.

460
00:16:02,390 --> 00:16:03,430
Get some rest.

461
00:16:04,270 --> 00:16:05,470
Bye-bye.

462
00:16:05,470 --> 00:16:07,060
(Looks back)

463
00:16:07,980 --> 00:16:09,140
I really...

464
00:16:09,140 --> 00:16:10,500
I was going to say goodnight,

465
00:16:10,500 --> 00:16:11,700
but I really just...

466
00:16:12,910 --> 00:16:13,990
couldn't bring myself to say it.

467
00:16:14,580 --> 00:16:15,860
(Laughs)

468
00:16:17,300 --> 00:16:20,860
(Looking at the photos)

469
00:16:21,630 --> 00:16:22,830
What am I doing?

470
00:16:27,380 --> 00:16:32,340
(Behind-the-Scenes 14)

471
00:16:43,300 --> 00:16:44,750
(Delicious)
It's delicious.

472
00:16:46,950 --> 00:16:48,150
What time did you go to bed last night?

473
00:16:48,150 --> 00:16:49,140
(Curious)

474
00:16:49,180 --> 00:16:49,940
(Remembering)

475
00:16:49,940 --> 00:16:50,580
Late at night.

476
00:16:51,140 --> 00:16:52,260
So do I.

477
00:16:53,100 --> 00:16:54,140
(Laughs)

478
00:16:54,190 --> 00:16:55,310
Why didn't you go to sleep?

479
00:16:55,310 --> 00:16:56,750
Didn't you say you'd go straight
to bed when you got back?

480
00:16:56,750 --> 00:16:59,180
Because we had to...

481
00:16:59,180 --> 00:17:00,220
well...

482
00:17:00,470 --> 00:17:01,510
take turns showering.

483
00:17:02,510 --> 00:17:03,990
Right, there are three of you.

484
00:17:04,270 --> 00:17:06,390
After showering,
we had to use the hair dryer.

485
00:17:07,100 --> 00:17:08,880
We had to wait for the last person
to finish drying their hair,

486
00:17:08,880 --> 00:17:10,030
then we'd all go to bed together.

487
00:17:12,870 --> 00:17:14,550
We're all very disciplined.

488
00:17:21,380 --> 00:17:26,340
(Behind-the-Scenes 15)

489
00:17:26,550 --> 00:17:28,110
Yu Yang, do you want some blueberries?

490
00:17:28,270 --> 00:17:28,670
Thanks.

491
00:17:29,190 --> 00:17:30,710
Just give this plate to Liang Renfang.

492
00:17:31,380 --> 00:17:32,140
Pour a little.

493
00:17:32,540 --> 00:17:33,380
Just give me a small amount.

494
00:17:33,780 --> 00:17:35,900
Careful.

495
00:17:35,900 --> 00:17:37,780
(Helps hold it)

496
00:17:40,420 --> 00:17:41,140
Okay.

497
00:17:41,510 --> 00:17:42,390
Is that all you're having?

498
00:17:42,390 --> 00:17:42,910
It's fine. That's enough.

499
00:17:43,500 --> 00:17:44,140
Thanks.

500
00:17:44,820 --> 00:17:45,900
This one is huge.

501
00:17:46,660 --> 00:17:47,460
Mutant version.

502
00:17:47,740 --> 00:17:48,540
Giant.

503
00:17:48,790 --> 00:17:49,870
(Repeating)
Giant blueberry.

504
00:17:52,780 --> 00:17:53,700
(Hands it over)
You eat it first.

505
00:17:53,900 --> 00:17:55,620
So what fruits do you usually like?

506
00:17:55,940 --> 00:17:56,940
Blueberries, mostly.

507
00:17:56,940 --> 00:17:57,820
You like blueberries too?

508
00:17:58,070 --> 00:17:58,590
Mm.

509
00:18:00,350 --> 00:18:02,140
We can play pool sometime.

510
00:18:02,140 --> 00:18:03,460
Sure, no problem.

511
00:18:03,980 --> 00:18:05,100
There's another expert here.

512
00:18:05,100 --> 00:18:05,900
An expert.

513
00:18:07,140 --> 00:18:07,780
Me?

514
00:18:08,390 --> 00:18:09,310
You're the one.

515
00:18:09,310 --> 00:18:10,430
There's another expert here.

516
00:18:10,750 --> 00:18:12,300
Of course.

517
00:18:12,300 --> 00:18:12,990
I can tell.

518
00:18:13,540 --> 00:18:15,180
There was a time when I was really into

519
00:18:15,180 --> 00:18:16,220
Chongqing hot pot.

520
00:18:16,780 --> 00:18:17,540
I loved it.

521
00:18:17,540 --> 00:18:18,140
Hot pot.

522
00:18:18,830 --> 00:18:20,310
But later, I realized

523
00:18:20,310 --> 00:18:21,070
it was just...

524
00:18:21,070 --> 00:18:21,820
Too spicy.

525
00:18:21,820 --> 00:18:22,660
I couldn't really handle it.

526
00:18:23,660 --> 00:18:25,580
The last one.

527
00:18:27,070 --> 00:18:27,980
Thanks.

528
00:18:30,390 --> 00:18:32,540
What time are you all
getting up tomorrow?

529
00:18:32,540 --> 00:18:34,820
I might have to get up
a little earlier than everyone else.

530
00:18:34,820 --> 00:18:37,020
Okay, then let's leave a little earlier
today so you can get up early tomorrow.

531
00:18:37,020 --> 00:18:37,980
Let's head out early.

532
00:18:37,980 --> 00:18:38,580
Let's go.

533
00:18:39,180 --> 00:18:41,140
(Offers to carry the guitar)

534
00:18:45,980 --> 00:18:50,940
(Behind-the-Scenes 16)

535
00:18:50,980 --> 00:18:52,580
(After the Newcomer's Privilege Date)

536
00:18:52,580 --> 00:18:54,790
(Asking)
How was it? Did today go by fast?

537
00:18:55,620 --> 00:18:56,500
It did.

538
00:18:56,500 --> 00:18:58,860
But the scenery today
was really beautiful.

539
00:19:00,220 --> 00:19:01,340
It's just that every time

540
00:19:01,340 --> 00:19:03,950
I pass through Beijing's old town,

541
00:19:04,270 --> 00:19:05,830
I have all sorts of thoughts.

542
00:19:07,900 --> 00:19:09,220
You kind of get immersed in it.

543
00:19:09,390 --> 00:19:11,470
For a moment, you're removed

544
00:19:11,470 --> 00:19:13,340
from your own reality,

545
00:19:13,340 --> 00:19:15,500
It's a more emotional kind of moment.

546
00:19:17,060 --> 00:19:19,020
You know there's
something called the blue hour?

547
00:19:19,220 --> 00:19:19,780
I do.

548
00:19:19,780 --> 00:19:21,820
(Blue Hour)
Yeah, I really love that feeling.

549
00:19:21,830 --> 00:19:23,500
Visually,

550
00:19:23,500 --> 00:19:25,380
it feels like everything
suddenly becomes clearer.

551
00:19:26,900 --> 00:19:28,900
It's a very subjective,
very personal feeling.

552
00:19:29,540 --> 00:19:30,900
(Agrees)
Yeah, exactly.

553
00:19:31,150 --> 00:19:32,220
It just feels like in the evening,

554
00:19:32,220 --> 00:19:33,260
your mind is more at ease.

555
00:19:33,510 --> 00:19:34,830
(Relaxed)
You become really relaxed,

556
00:19:34,830 --> 00:19:35,790
and some of that

557
00:19:35,910 --> 00:19:36,910
anxiety fades away.

558
00:19:37,260 --> 00:19:39,620
It's the clarity with which
you see everything.

559
00:19:40,060 --> 00:19:42,060
It's just that in the evening,
there's still light,

560
00:19:42,060 --> 00:19:43,790
but the light is very...

561
00:19:45,230 --> 00:19:46,340
very soft.

562
00:19:46,340 --> 00:19:47,460
So

563
00:19:47,460 --> 00:19:48,380
at that moment,

564
00:19:48,380 --> 00:19:50,460
a lot of things we couldn't see before

565
00:19:50,460 --> 00:19:51,620
suddenly come into view.

566
00:19:51,620 --> 00:19:52,500
(As the white light warms,
everything reveals its true form)

567
00:19:52,500 --> 00:19:52,900
Exactly.

568
00:19:56,060 --> 00:20:01,020
(Behind-the-Scenes 17)

